(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Whitehead Field Dynamics and Reconfiguration Graphs of Cubic Multigraphs\
\>", "Title",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Suppressed" -> 
     "True"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"440c932d-7121-bffe-49bc-67861f652e48"],

Cell["Alexander Kolpakov", "Author",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Suppressed" -> 
     "True"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"9ec6d886-361f-56c5-e080-3cb742d6cdbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\G_N"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"f8365500-3997-7a5e-84a1-64cf319998a3"],
 " be the graph whose vertices are isomorphism classes of connected\ncubic \
multigraphs on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "30fbf617-dfc5-cd4e-1a2c-896e84343178"],
 " vertices, with edges generated by Whitehead moves.  We\nput over each \
class ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\gamma=[G]"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"0b84ae95-54a2-05df-3017-65708269d669"],
 " the fibre ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["F", "\[Gamma]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["C", "0"], "(", "G", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\F_\\gamma=C^0(G)"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"50e750a5-1a7e-eab6-e5bd-a284620572e1"],
 " and transport a\nscalar field by averaging the two endpoint values of the \
edge on which the\nWhitehead move is performed.  This produces a random \
product of local\northogonal projections, followed by settlement \
permutations.  The resulting\ndynamics has a clean Lyapunov function, the \
variance above the constant mode,\nand a noninvertible, semigroup-valued \
cocycle on a non-canonically trivialized\nfield bundle over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\G_N"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"acab95ec-ec39-cd60-6eeb-1537a2676216"],
 ".  We identify the exact configuration-model stationary\nlaw of the \
local-move chain, prove a settlement-independent quenched exponent\nupper \
bound of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     SuperscriptBox["N", "3"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "-N^{-3}"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"130bb503-5e0c-a2aa-5d85-8293c1965907"],
 ", and combine a spectral-average inequality with the\nconfiguration-model \
Friedman theorem to obtain a stationary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["c", "N"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "-c/N"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"bc5b6aef-1dda-f505-6eb1-ac8bbc160b5a"],
 " upper\nbound on the top norm Lyapunov exponent.  On the persistent \
labelled lift we\nalso find exact finite-time consensus, and hence exponent \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "-\\infty"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"12cd61b2-2227-fd03-a420-d425da3b904c"],
 ", at\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["N", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "2"}], ",", "4", ",", "8"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N=2,4,8"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"6acbc9cf-a7ed-9512-5949-43f8ff27a313"],
 ".  For the three graphs of Whitehead moves we derive a quadratic\nfamily of \
low labelled modes, an exact loop-count Dirichlet form and sharp\nbridge \
asymptotics for the multiplicity chain, and exact feature and field\n\
obstructions for the simple support.  Gauge-covariant square defects remain\n\
useful local observables, but immediate backtracking already shows why these\n\
transports are not an ordinary connection.  Complete unlabelled enumeration\n\
through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"N", "\[LongEqual]", "14"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N=14"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"762abec7-7431-4b74-444a-de46838e4053"],
 " separates proved asymptotics from finite conjectures."
}], "Abstract",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Environment" -> "abstract", "EnvironmentOpen" -> "\\begin{abstract}", 
     "Trailing" -> "", "BodyIndent" -> "\n", "EnvironmentClose" -> 
     "\n\\end{abstract}", "Separator" -> 
     "\n\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"049de847-48b0-cd2c-ad20-cf35749000d2"],

Cell["Introduction and contributions", "Section",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Indent" -> "", "Trailing" -> "", "Separator" -> 
     "\n\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"6be4a4b2-1956-3a1c-e529-40cb68c7e1c2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fix an even integer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a3ae36f-2d6f-c1b2-64d8-7b3e83bd65fb"],
 ". Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\C_N"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"71b59ac0-1556-f57b-37c0-29e4fd63f4bf"],
 " be the finite set of connected cubic\nmultigraphs on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "f1c09542-1fb3-20a4-82d9-ae156ea65394"],
 " vertices, considered up to isomorphism unless labels are\nexplicitly \
introduced. Loops and multiple edges are allowed; a loop contributes\ntwo to \
the degree. In addition to the carrier graph itself, there are three\n\
graph-of-graphs conventions on this material. Li's labelled simple graph has\n\
fixed-labelled cubic graphs as vertices and collapses repeated moves to the\n\
same labelled target.  Grave de Peralta--Kolpakov's directed multigraph has\n\
unlabelled classes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", 
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "[G]"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "71077e40-eba5-73d0-4f91-6f9a93297cbf"],
 " as vertices and retains one directed slot for each\nunlabelled Whitehead \
resolution, including multiplicity and self-slots.\nFinally, the unlabelled \
simple-support graph has the same class vertices but\ncollapses all positive \
nonself multiplicities to one undirected edge. We use\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\G_N"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"4f23e370-a5cd-a390-2a1a-5c78a706b06f"],
 " only when the accompanying text specifies the edge convention; every\n\
degree, Laplacian, stationary law, and ball is indexed by its underlying\n\
object."
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Separator" -> 
     "\n\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"229622e5-535b-7c32-c51a-52a36d34fd80"],

Cell["\<\
The four state-and-clock conventions used below are summarized as follows.
{\\small\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"5c21e517-17aa-d63f-3f6b-8d5410ee5eae"],

