Cell["\<\
In the half-edge model, each Whitehead move only reassigns the four \
half-edges
incident to the endpoints of the selected edge and not belonging to that \
edge.
Disjoint endpoint sets give disjoint local data, so the graph rewrites commute.
The field operators also commute because the averaging projections act on
disjoint coordinate pairs.  Thus both two-step path transports are identical,
up to the same final settlement.\
\>", "Proof",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Environment" -> "proof", "EnvironmentOpen" -> "\\begin{proof}", 
     "Trailing" -> "", "BodyIndent" -> "\n", "EnvironmentClose" -> 
     "\n\\end{proof}", "Separator" -> 
     "\n\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"863276ca-0388-de61-ed1d-88f62ec8c89b"],

Cell["\<\
Incident squares are the basic non-flat squares.  Their defect is not only a
property of the cubic graph rewrite; it also includes the averaging \
operators.
Locally, when the two consecutive averaged pairs share one vertex, the
commutator has singular values\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"d1e6cc13-69bd-779f-97fd-54943aca7092"],

