     "\n\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"f2b37974-0ed8-7256-cd46-a1427aab3f6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The proof also explains why the bridged bottleneck does not automatically\n\
destroy finite-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "3811467a-03a9-8ebd-2dfa-d935716e64db"],
 " field relaxation.  A successful block may pass through\nbridged graphs and \
may average bridge edges.  That is fine: the block contracts\nbecause the \
list of averaged label-pairs contains a spanning tree, not because\nthe \
intermediate base graphs avoid bottlenecks."
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Separator" -> 
     "\n\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"232b1177-bfe2-9e86-8f7c-2590589a9719"],

